### Tested versions

Reproducible in 4.6.2

### System information

Godot v4.6.2.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.92 GiB memory

### Issue description

There are two scenarios in which `AStarGrid2D.get_id_path(...)` returns an empty list:

* if no path exists between the origin and destination (i.e. pathfinding failed)
* if the origin and destination are adjacent to one another (i.e. the path was successfully resolved and has no intermediate nodes)

This means that if I get an empty list from the AStarGrid2D, I then have to check myself if pathfinding has failed or succeeded. This is relatively easy when diagonal movement is disabled or unconditionally enabled, as I only need to check that the distance between the grid coordinates is <= 1.0 or <= sqrt(1.0). However, if diagonal moves are conditionally enabled (with DIAGONAL_MODE_AT_LEAST_ONE_WALKABLE or DIAGONAL_MODE_ONLY_IF_NO_OBSTACLES), I need to replicate logic that should be encapsulated within the AStarGrid2D class within my game logic just to tell if pathfinding has succeeded:

```
            ResolvedPath = AStarGrid2D.get_id_path(current, Destination).ToList();
            if (ResolvedPath.Count != 0) {
                IsPathResolved = true;
            }
            else if (
                (current - Destination).Length() <= Globals.TILE_SIZE.Length() &&
                gameMap.IsPassable(new Vector2I(current.X, Destination.Y)) &&
                gameMap.IsPassable(new Vector2I(Destination.X, current.Y))
            ) {
                IsPathResolved = true;
            }
```

### Steps to reproduce

Call "AStarGrid2D.get_id_path(...)"

